{
 "about": "The Voyager 2 frames of Neptune for its haze, from the PDS Ring-Moon Systems Node (OPUS): the wide-angle camera's Blue, Green and Orange frames of the limb at 152 degrees of phase, an hour and a half after closest approach (role close); the narrow-angle camera's Clear frames of the same stretch of limb minutes later, and of the limb at 136 degrees twelve hours after it (role clear); and its complete Blue, Green and Orange sets of the crescent at 133 degrees, six days after it (role departure). Latitudes are planetocentric and longitudes east (OPUS gives IAU west longitudes); distance is to Neptune's centre, resolution is at the centre of the disk, in km a raw pixel.",
